{
  "dom_id": "step-q161527",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=⟨5t,\\,\\frac{1}{(t+2)^{2}},\\,{e}^{t}+t⟩.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $5t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\frac{1}{(t+2)^{2}}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${e}^{t}+t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242901/assets/b50ca0dfe2d2fa5a56edd03e9e4817751f821d610faba2e2dd3eb07982157a4a.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,\\infty ).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
